{
  "id": "lifecycle-phases-lifecycle-phases",
  "slug": "lifecycle-phases",
  "title": "Lifecycle Phases",
  "category": "Build Tools",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-maven-build-lifecycle",
      "heading": "What is Maven Build Lifecycle?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A Build Lifecycle in Maven is a sequence of phases that define the order and tasks involved in building and managing a project."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 23,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "why-is-build-lifecycle-important",
          "heading": "Why is Build Lifecycle Important?",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Automates the build process by executing tasks in predefined order.",
                "Reduces the number of commands developers need to remember.",
                "Helps in compiling, testing, packaging, and deploying the application consistently.",
                "Handles project documentation and cleaning previous builds."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 36,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "three-built-in-maven-lifecycles",
          "heading": "Three Built-In Maven Lifecycles",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": true,
              "items": [
                "clean – Cleans the previous build",
                "default – The main lifecycle for building and deploying",
                "site – Generates project documentation"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Each lifecycle contains phases, which are executed in sequence."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 29,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clean-lifecycle",
      "heading": "Clean Lifecycle",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Cleans the project for fresh builds"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Phase",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "pre-clean",
              "Executes tasks before actual project cleaning begins"
            ],
            [
              "clean",
              "Deletes outputs of previous build (typically target/ folder)"
            ],
            [
              "post-clean",
              "Final clean-up steps after removing build artifacts"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Apache Maven/Lifecycle Phases/Lifecycle%20Phases/image.png",
          "alt": "image.png",
          "originalPath": "Lifecycle%20Phases/image.png"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Command to run:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "bash",
          "code": "mvn clean",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 36,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "default-lifecycle",
      "heading": "Default Lifecycle",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Core lifecycle for building the application"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This is the most commonly used lifecycle with 23 phases, out of which the important ones are:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Phase",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "validate",
              "Checks the correctness of the project structure (e.g., checks for presence of pom.xml)"
            ],
            [
              "compile",
              "Compiles .java source files into .class bytecode (stored in target/)"
            ],
            [
              "test",
              "Runs unit tests using testing frameworks like JUnit; outputs go to target/surefire-reports/"
            ],
            [
              "package",
              "Bundles compiled code and resources into a JAR/WAR/EAR file"
            ],
            [
              "verify",
              "Performs additional checks (e.g., integration test validation)"
            ],
            [
              "install",
              "Installs the packaged artifact into the local repository for reuse in other local Maven projects"
            ],
            [
              "deploy",
              "Deploys the artifact to a remote repository (e.g., Nexus, Artifactory) for sharing across teams"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Apache Maven/Lifecycle Phases/Lifecycle%20Phases/image%201.png",
          "alt": "image.png",
          "originalPath": "Lifecycle%20Phases/image%201.png"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Command to run the full build process:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "bash",
          "code": "mvn install",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "➡️ This will implicitly run all previous phases in order (validate → deploy)."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 132,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "site-lifecycle",
      "heading": "Site Lifecycle",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Generates documentation for the project"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Used for reporting and documentation, this lifecycle involves generating a project website."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Phase",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "pre-site",
              "Prepares before generating the site"
            ],
            [
              "site",
              "Generates the project's site documentation (target/site/)"
            ],
            [
              "post-site",
              "Finalizes and prepares site content"
            ],
            [
              "site-deploy",
              "Deploys site documentation to a web server (optional)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Command to generate site:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "bash",
          "code": "mvn site",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 51,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "key-concepts-summary",
      "heading": "Key Concepts Summary",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "-lifecycle",
          "heading": "🔁 Lifecycle",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A sequence of phases that Maven follows to build a project."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 11,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "-phase",
          "heading": "⚙️ Phase",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A step within the lifecycle. Executing a later phase implicitly runs all prior phases."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 14,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "-target-folder",
          "heading": "📁 Target Folder",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Location where Maven stores compiled code and packaged artifacts (${basedir}/target)."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 10,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "-surefire-reports",
          "heading": "🧪 Surefire Reports",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Test result reports are placed here:"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "target/surefire-reports/"
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 7,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "developer-tips",
      "heading": "Developer Tips",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Run mvn compile to only compile.",
            "Run mvn test to compile and run tests.",
            "Run mvn clean install to clean and build the entire project fresh.",
            "Run mvn site to generate documentation for your project."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 35,
      "subsections": []
    }
